    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d451">

                <pb facs="0387" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/555: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-31T15:00:00-00:44">March 31, 1942—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. From McBride. Agreement signed today.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d451-f1"/> Am
                    departing tonight on TWA stratoliner for Washington.</p>
                <p>Department’s 75, March 29, 4 p.m.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d451-f2"/> President
                    Barclay consents to RAF refueling at Fisherman Lake on following conditions:</p>
                <p>That planes refuel only and take off as soon as possible, crews to wear civilian
                    clothes, consent granted temporarily until airports in Liberia can be defended
                    by American forces. Colonel Kemp at Accra informed. [McBride.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d451-f1" n="21" xml:id="d451-f1-content">
                <p>For text, see Department of State Executive Agreement Series No. 275, or 56 Stat.
                    (pt. 2) 1621.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d451-f2" n="22" xml:id="d451-f2-content">
